     5034551.337252083
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 4 · CIESIN / SEDAC – SYR final data (panels c, d)",
     "markdown": "🟡 **PARTIAL** – exists but incomplete or not verifiable from here\n\nSYR figure data are catalogued in the IPCC Data Catalogue and hosted by CIESIN / NASA SEDAC (Columbia University).\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Panel (c)** | *SYR LR Figure 2.1 (c): Changes in global surface temperature* · id 8498 · v1.0.0 (2025-04-10) · doi 10.7927/nq55-cr83 · Excel ~15 KB |\n| **Panel (d)** | *SYR LR Figure 2.1 (d): Humans are responsible* · id 8493 · v1.0.0 (2025-04-09) · doi 10.7927/b38b-zp83 – verify on landing page |\n| **Panels (a), (b)** | 🔴 no SYR-level record – use WGIII SPM.1 / WGI Fig 2.5 |\n| **Access** | sedac.ciesin.columbia.edu/ddc/ar6-syr-lr-fig2-1c/ and …-1d/ – browser only |\n| **Open item** | download both workbooks, confirm DOI and licence, save as CSV in `data/final/syr_fig2_1/` |\n\n➡ **Next** – the status dashboard.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "0f51b392-28f1-49e4-883b-355226f5b091": {
   "name": "Data status at a glance",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 1.4,
    "extent": [
     -34478035.576546915,
     -20223937.14614873,
     36704425.39241239,
     27231036.833157476
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "Data status at a glance",
     "markdown": "## Where Figure 2.1 stands today\n\n| Tier → panel | (a) emissions | (b) concentr. | (c) temperature | (d) attribution |\n|---|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n| **1** Report (ipcc.ch) | 🔵 | 🔵 | 🔵 | 🔵 |\n| **2** Input · DDC at DKRZ (CMIP6) | – | – | 🔵 | 🔵 |\n| **2** Input · originating institutions | 🔵 | 🔵 | 🟢 | 🔵 |\n| **3** Intermediate · chapter records at CEDA | 🟡 | 🟢 | 🟢 | 🟢 |\n| **4** Final · Working Group record | 🟢 | 🟢 | 🟢 | 🟢 |\n| **4** Final · SYR record (SEDAC) | 🔴 | 🔴 | 🟡 | 🟡 |\n\n🟢 available · 🔵 online · 🟡 partial · 🔴 missing · checked 2026-10-13\n\n\n### What changed on 2026-10-13\n* CEDA catalogue reachable again → every CEDA DOI verified (all **citable**, all resolve).\n* Four chapter-level CEDA records added → tier 3 is 🟢 for panels (b), (c), (d).\n* CEDA *Input data for Figure 2.11* added → the four observational datasets behind panel (c).\n* Notebook now loads CEDA files **live** (CORS enabled), falling back to the bundled copies.\n\n### Still open\n* SYR workbooks (c), (d) at SEDAC – browser only.\n* DKRZ Supplements list – JavaScript only.\n* CEDA SYR collection record – not yet published.\n\n➡ **Next** – how to do this for any IPCC figure.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "29fa82ad-9bad-4957-99dc-66eed1e7ab74": {
   "name": "How to reuse the data",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 1.4,
    "extent": [
     -34478035.576546915,
     -20223937.14614873,
     36704425.39241239,
     27231036.833157476
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "How to reuse the data",
     "markdown": "## From any IPCC figure to its data\n\n1. **Read the caption's traceability tag** – it names the source figures.\n2. **Final data first** – WGI/WGII → CEDA `10.5285/…` · WGIII → IPCC Data Catalogue `10.48490/…` · SYR → SEDAC `10.7927/…`.\n3. **Open the README and licence** shipped with the record (CEDA: BADC-CSV).\n4. **Need the chain?** Look for chapter-level and *input data* records at CEDA, DKRZ Supplements, and code on github.com/IPCC-WG1.\n5. **Need raw inputs?** CMIP6 at DKRZ; observations and inventories at the producing institutions.\n6. **Cite twice** – dataset DOI *and* report component. Redraw figures from data (images are IPCC copyright).\n\n**In this project**\n* `ar6_syr_fig2_1_data_story.ipynb` – reproduces the four panels live in the browser.\n* `data/PROVENANCE.md` – every record, version, DOI, licence.\n* `README.md` – open items.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  }
 },
